    "content": "Many studies have investigated how to improve LLM reasoning without fine-tuning models [10,13, 14, 12]. A common approach that consistently shows improvement is prompt engineering,where one uses the system prompt to specify how the model should approach a problem. Chain-of-Thought [10, 15] is a familiar example, and it often asks the model to work step-by-step through atask. Algorithm-of-Thought [12] is another approach that instructs the model to think like a searchalgorithm. Other works seek to decompose the problem [16, 14], allowing the model to exploreseveral reasoning branches and then proceed with the most promising one based on a heuristic such",
